  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The Anatomy Lesson: Unveiling the Fasciculus Medicinae has ten main sections, corresponding to the ten wooodcuts found in the 1495 Fasciculus Medicinae ..." -- editorial note.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Joyce Cutler-Shaw and Robin Price developed The Anatomy Lesson: Unveiling the Fasciculus Medicinae over the course of a decade, beginning in 1994 ... Boxcar Press made the eighty-five photopolymer plates from which the book was printed. The cotton text sheets were handmade by John and Kathy Koller ... Editing and letterpress printing was done by Robin Price, with much assistance from Anne Thompson, at the Starr Mill in Middletown, Connecticut. The hologram on the cover ... features an early-eighteenth-century brass lancet ... The company Pina Zangaro fabricated and engraved the custom stainless steel boxes that house the book. The concertina binding was co-designed by Daniel E. Kelm, Price, and Cutler-Shaw ... In an edition of fifty, this is number ..." -- colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Place of publication from publisher's prospectus and colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
